            <ArticleTitle>Use of EMLA cream in the treatment of post-herpetic neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>EMLA cream is an acronym for eutectic mixture of local anesthetics. It contains lidocaine and prilocaine creams. A eutectic preparation, applied topically, penetrates into the dermis after an application period of 1 to 2 hours. This case report describes the successful treatment with EMLA cream of post-herpetic neuralgia, which was resistant to other modes of therapy, and briefly discusses the pharmacology of EMLA cream.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
